{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Sally in Spain", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "A Travel Journal", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 8, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Celebrating Important Occasions > Running of the Bulls", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Placeholder", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Placeholder", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Writing A Travel Journal", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You write a travel journal to document and remember new places, cultures and experiences.<br/><br/>A travel journal is similar to a diary.  They are usually small enough to carry in your hand luggage while you travel.<br/>You usually use the Simple Past tense when you write in a travel journal because you usually write about things after they happen.<br/>A travel diary entry often includes:<br/><br/><li>A location and date in the title<br/><li>Who you traveled with<br/><li>Where you stayed and if you enjoyed it<br/><li>Who you met and their contact information<br/><li>Places to eat and your comments<br/><li>Things to see and if you would visit again<br/><br/>Sometimes, a travel journal entry can be about an experience like watching the \u201cRunning of the Bulls\u201d or another event.<br/><br/>Your travel diary should have enough detail for you to visit an area again.", "type": "describer"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use in a travel journal.", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "engenn4le05ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "barrier  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " something that prevents or blocks movement from one place to another ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There were barriers along the sides of the street.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le05ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to chase", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the act of following and trying to catch ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The bulls were chasing the men.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le05ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "suddenly ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very quickly in an unexpected way ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Suddenly, hundreds of people started filling the streets.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le05ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to explore  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to go through a place to learn more about it  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I decided to explore the city.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le05ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "herd  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a large group of the same animal", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A herd of bulls chased the men down the street. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le05ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to trample  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to tread on or crush ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The bulls trampled the man.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le05ob08aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Interview a friend or family member about a holiday or vacation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask these questions: <ul><li>What was the location and date of your trip?</li> <li>Who did you travel with?</li> <li>Where did you stay? Did you enjoy it?</li> <li>Who did you meet? Did you get their contact information?</li> <li>Where did you eat? Was it good?</li> <li>What would you see again if you returned?</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Use this information to write their travel diary.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I interview a friend or family member about a vacation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask questions about their holiday.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a travel journal for another person.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write complete statements about travel.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Vocabulary and Grammar", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "I can write about what I did.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can express opinions about other people and things in a written way.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can write a short travel journal.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Are you a thrill seeker? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "Do you like to do things that are dangerous like skydiving or do you prefer activities that are not dangerous?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [